# Normalize line endings to LF in both the repository and the working tree.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system config, which checks
# out CRLF on Windows. The repository already stores LF, so nothing is broken -
# but gofmt treats CRLF as unformatted and flags every .go file, which buries
# real formatting problems in noise. Pinning eol=lf makes host-side gofmt a
# usable signal and keeps the Windows and macOS checkouts identical.
#
# text=auto still detects binary files and leaves them untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
